> 
> That's a very iffy use of ju'o cu'i; I'm not at all sure that ju'o cu'i
> is strong enough to eliminate the identicality of no'u.

It isn't meant to eliminate the identicality, it just flags it
as a possibility. I'm not sure ju'ocu'i is the best choice here,
but cumki doesn't seem right to me.  

> > mulpi'i: x1 pilji x2 x3 ije x1 e x2 e x3 mulnau
> 
> You mean mulna'u there, yes? 

Yes, sorry.

> Why not just use pilji?

Because we only want integer factors. 

> > i.e. "x1 is divisible by x2"
> 
